## 2. Combine Algorithm (Exact Math)

Per query row \(i\) (flattened `(seqlen, head)` index), across splits \(s \in \{0,\ldots,S-1\}\):

### Step A — Load per-split LSEs, compute global LSE

From kernel Step 4 (`flash_fwd_combine_kernel.h:574–610`):

```574:610:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_combine_kernel.h
        // Step 4: compute the final LSE along the split dimension
        ...
        for (int m = 0; m < size<2>(ts2rrLSE); ++m) {
            float lse_max = ts2rrLSE(_0{}, _0{}, m);
            for (int s = 1; s < size<1>(ts2rrLSE); ++s) { lse_max = max(lse_max, ts2rrLSE(_0{}, s, m)); }
            ...
            lse_max = Allreduce<kSmemThreadsPerColLSEt>::run(lse_max, max_op);
            ...
            float lse_max_cur = lse_max == -INFINITY ? 0.0f : lse_max;
            float lse_sum_cur = 0.f;
            for (int s = 0; s < size<1>(ts2rrLSE); ++s) {
                float scale = expf(ts2rrLSE(_0{}, s, m) - lse_max_cur);
                lse_sum_cur += scale;
                ts2rrLSE(_0{}, s, m) = scale;
            }
            lse_sum_cur = Allreduce<kSmemThreadsPerColLSEt>::run(lse_sum_cur, sum_op);
            lse_sum(m) = logf(lse_sum_cur) + lse_max;
            float inv_sum = (lse_sum_cur == 0.f || lse_sum_cur != lse_sum_cur) ? 0.f : 1.f / lse_sum_cur;
            for (int s = 0; s < size<1>(ts2rrLSE); ++s) { ts2rrLSE(_0{}, s, m) *= inv_sum; }
        }
```

**Math:**

\[
\text{lse\_max}_i = \max_s \text{LSE}_{i,s}
\]

\[
\text{unnorm\_weight}_{i,s} = \exp(\text{LSE}_{i,s} - \text{lse\_max}_i)
\]

\[
\text{lse\_global}_i = \log\!\Big(\sum_s \text{unnorm\_weight}_{i,s}\Big) + \text{lse\_max}_i
\]

\[
\text{weight}_{i,s} = \frac{\text{unnorm\_weight}_{i,s}}{\sum_s \text{unnorm\_weight}_{i,s}} = \exp(\text{LSE}_{i,s} - \text{lse\_global}_i)
\]

Weights are stored back to `smem_lse` for the O accumulation loop.

### Step B — Weighted sum of partial O, write final O

```646:687:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_combine_kernel.h
        // Step 6: read O_partial from gmem -> smem -> rmem and accumulate the final O
        ...
        for (int s = 0; s <= thr_max_valid_split; ++s) {
            ...
            for (int m = 0; m < size<1>(tOrOpartial); ++m) { scale(m) = sLSE(s, get<0>(tOcO(_0{}, m, _0{}))); }
            ...
            for (int m = 0; m < size<1>(tOrOpartial); ++m) {
                if (tObidh(m) >= 0 && scale(m) > 0.f) {
                    for (int k = 0; k < size<2>(tOrOpartial); ++k) {
                        ...
                        tOrO(i, m, k) += scale(m) * rOpartial[i];
                    }
                }
            }
        }
```

**Math:**

\[
O_i = \sum_s \text{weight}_{i,s} \cdot O^{\text{partial}}_{i,s}
\]

No additional normalization — `O_partial` is already split-local softmax-normalized; combine only reweights by global softmax masses.

Final O is cast from fp32 accumulator to output dtype (bf16/fp16) before store (lines 690–710).

**Note:** Combine uses `expf`/`logf`, **not** `exp2f`/`log2f` (those are used in the fwd mainloop softmax only).

