## 4. Launch Configuration

### Grid / block

```227:231:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_combine_kernel.h
        static dim3 get_grid_shape(SchedulerArguments const& args) {
            unsigned int num_blocks_k = cute::ceil_div(args.dv, kBlockK);
            unsigned int num_blocks_m = cute::ceil_div(args.seqlen_q * args.num_heads, kBlockM);
            return {num_blocks_m, num_blocks_k, static_cast<unsigned int>(args.b)};
        }
```

| Dim | Maps to |
|-----|---------|
| `grid.x` | M-tile over flattened `(seqlen_q × num_heads)` |
| `grid.y` | K-tile over head dim `dv` |
| `grid.z` | batch (or virtual batch for varlen) |
| `block` | **256 threads** |

Varlen has two schedulers — if grid >50% sparse, **linearizes (batch, M)** into `grid.x` with `grid.z=1` (lines 241–320).

### kMaxSplits template selection

```71:85:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_combine_launch_template.h
            if constexpr (kBlockM >= 16) {
                if (params.num_splits <= 16) {
                    run_flash_fwd_combine<Arch, kBlockM, kBlockK, 4, ...>(...);  // kMaxSplits=16
                    return;
                }
            }
            if (params.num_splits <= 32) {
                run_flash_fwd_combine<..., 5, ...>(...);  // kMaxSplits=32
            } else if (params.num_splits <= 64) {
                run_flash_fwd_combine<..., 6, ...>(...);  // kMaxSplits=64
            } else if (params.num_splits <= 128) {
                run_flash_fwd_combine<..., 7, ...>(...);  // kMaxSplits=128
            } else {
                run_flash_fwd_combine<..., 8, ...>(...);  // kMaxSplits=256
            }
```

`kMaxSplits = 1 << kLogMaxSplits` (line 33). Larger `kMaxSplits` → larger LSE smem (`kMaxSplits × kBlockM` floats), fixed at compile time. Constraint: `kBlockM==8` cannot use `kLogMaxSplits=4` (16 splits) because `kMaxSplits % num_LSE_load_rows == 0` assert fails — hence the `kBlockM >= 16` guard (line 71).

Smem size can exceed 48 KB → dynamic smem requested (lines 55–57 launch template).

### Thread-to-element mapping

Each CTA owns one `(m_block, k_block, batch)` tile:
- Covers rows `[m_block*kBlockM, …)` of `(seqlen, head)` flatten
- Covers cols `[k_block*kBlockK, …)` of head dim
- All splits processed serially within the CTA for those rows/cols
- LSE final write only from `k_block == 0` (lines 624–644)

