```

### Device level (combine kernel)

```453:454:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_combine_kernel.h
        int const num_splits = params.num_splits_dynamic_ptr ? params.num_splits_dynamic_ptr[maybe_virtual_batch] : get<1>(params.shape_LSE_partial);
        if (num_splits <= 1) { return; }
```

Also early exit for out-of-range M-tiles (line 451) and invalid batch (443).

### Fwd kernel fast paths when not splitting

- Epilogue writes directly to `O`/`LSE` (TMA store on SM90 dense non-split)
- `Use_smem = !(Split && !Varlen)` — dense split skips epilogue smem, writes fp32 partials directly from registers (line 37 epilogue)

