## 6. CUTLASS/CuTe vs Hand-Portable

### CUTLASS/CuTe (need reimplementation or thin wrappers)

| Component | Location | Portability |
|-----------|----------|-------------|
| CuTe `Tensor`, `Layout`, `make_tiled_copy`, `partition_*` | Throughout combine kernel | Logic portable; API is CuTe-specific |
| `Copy_Atom<SM80_CP_ASYNC_*>` | lines 52–87 | **Portable** — maps to `cp.async` PTX |
| `cutlass::FastDivmod` | lines 173, 456 | Trivial portable replacement |
| `cutlass::arch::wait_on_dependent_grids` | lines 428, 472 | **SM90 PDL PTX** (`griddepcontrol.wait`) |
| `cutlass::device_kernel` / `kernel_launch` with PDL | launch template 53–59 | Launch wrapper only |
| CuTe `Swizzle<>` for LSE smem | lines 92–101 | Replicate swizzle pattern manually |
| `cutlass::NumericArrayConverter` via `convert_type_out` | utils.h:192–204 | Standard dtype conversion |

### Raw / easily portable

| Component | Notes |
|-----------|-------|
| **Algorithm** (LSE max, exp weights, weighted O sum) | Pure CUDA, ~30 lines core math |
| **`Allreduce<N>` warp shuffles** | `utils.h:78–97` — copy verbatim |
| **cp.async 4-stage ring buffer** | Standard Ampere+ pattern |
| **256-thread block, 128-bit vector loads** | No special HW beyond cp.async |
| **No TMA, no WGMMA** in combine | Combine is the most portable part of FA3 |

### Not in combine (don't need for this kernel)

- TMA descriptors, mbarrier pipelines, WGMMA — fwd mainloop only
- Cluster, persistent tile scheduler — fwd only

